Example programs
================

Small programs to build against CGTK, each in a directory of its own
with a Makefile.

All but glarea/ come from the GTK+ 1.2 tutorial, whose text is no
longer shipped. They show the API as GTK+ 1.2 had it, which CGTK
keeps, and build and run unchanged. None of them uses what CGTK adds.
glarea/ is CGTK's own, for GtkGLArea.

Building
--------

The Makefiles use gtk-config, which has to be on PATH; for a prefix the
dynamic linker does not search, see "Finding the libraries at run time"
in ../INSTALL.

"make" here builds every example but glarea/, which needs OpenGL and
is built by "make" in glarea/. "make clean" removes what was built.

The programs
------------

  base/             the smallest program: an empty window
  helloworld/       a window with a button that quits it
  helloworld2/      two buttons sharing one callback
  packbox/          how boxes pack their children: run it with 1, 2 or 3
  table/            buttons placed in a GtkTable
  buttons/          a button holding a picture and a label
  radiobuttons/     a group of radio buttons
  rangewidgets/     scales and scrollbars sharing adjustments, with
                    their options in menus
  entry/            a GtkEntry, editable or not, its text shown or hidden
  spinbutton/       spin buttons for dates and for numbers
  calendar/         GtkCalendar and its options
  progressbar/      a progress bar, with its text and activity mode
  statusbar/        messages pushed onto and popped from a status bar
  text/             GtkText, editable or not, words wrapped or not
  clist/            GtkCList in a scrolled window
  list/             GtkList, and a frame its selected item can be put in
  tree/             GtkTree with subtrees
  notebook/         a notebook: turning and removing pages, moving the tabs
  menu/             a menu bar built by hand (menu.c) and by GtkItemFactory
                    (itemfactory.c)
  filesel/          the file selector
  frame/            a GtkFrame and its label
  aspectframe/      a frame that keeps its child's proportions
  paned/            a pane divided between a list and a text
  scrolledwin/      a table of buttons in a scrolled window
  fixed/            buttons that move about a GtkFixed
  packer/           GtkPacker and its options
  eventbox/         an event box catching clicks on a label
  rulers/           rulers that follow the pointer over a drawing area
  scribble-simple/  drawing with the pointer into a pixmap
  pixmap/           a picture from XPM data on a button
  wheelbarrow/      a shaped window: a wheelbarrow with no frame
  selection/        asking for the targets of the primary selection
                    (gettargets.c) and claiming it (setselection.c)
  tictactoe/        a composite widget made of other widgets
  gtkdial/          a widget drawn from scratch: a dial
  glarea/           GtkGLArea: glarea.c with the GL of glBegin and glEnd,
                    as programs for GTK+ 1.2's GtkGLArea used it;
                    glcore.c with a GL 3.3 core profile context; and
                    glloop.c drawing without pause from the main loop

find-examples.sh prints the examples' files in the form the top
Makefile.am's EXTRA_DIST lists them, for when examples are added or
removed.
